  "summary": "Design delivered as the issue comment (5394942824), no product code, no cards filed. The card's premise holds: none of the four legs is cross-request cached on main today, and the invalidation design was genuinely undecided. But ONE named sub-direction it inherited from #10757 is FORECLOSED and I did not design around it: direction 1 (leg A, 'enable better-auth cookieCache or secondaryStorage') collides with #4785, which is CLOSED as completed via merged PR #5101 fixing the session of record as sys_session, and is pinned by plugin-auth/src/session-of-record.test.ts whose tests are named 'opting into cacheSecondaryStorage empties sys_session and makes idle timeout inert', 'option C (dual-write) is not reachable through config', and 'the DEFAULT composition refuses to boot with a secondaryStorage rather than degrading quietly'. So leg A splits: its customSession half is DELETED by #10348-C and should be served by leg B's cache rather than designed separately, and its better-auth half is a decision surface (re-open #4785), not a cache-design surface. Design core: the unit is 'a cached answer plus the contract that says when it stops being an answer' -- write-invalidation at the ObjectQL engine middleware seam as primary (measured: better-auth's own adapter routes insert/update/delete through the engine, so one seam catches membership/ban/session/org-role writes; plugin-security already does exactly this with writeEpoch ahead of the isSystem bypass), plus a TTL as the bound. Multi-node is not a fork for grants: the ONLY shipped cross-node channel is IPubSub and it is at-most-once with no replay by its own doc, so a bus can never be the correctness mechanism -- it narrows the typical window, the TTL bounds the worst case. Recommend adding an authz.invalidated channel on the existing bus following MetadataClusterBridgePlugin's shape, plus a LOUD boot posture statement when a grants cache is on with no bus (a silently-absent bridge is exactly #4785's failure shape). Three constraints a naive keying gets wrong are called out with evidence: (B.1) ADR-0091 validity windows are evaluated at resolution time, so a cached envelope FREEZES an expiry -- no write happens at that boundary, so write-invalidation is blind to it by construction and an entry must expire at min(ttl, nextBoundary); I found this stated nowhere in the #10757 lineage. (B.2) seedPermissions/seedEmail are part of the answer and their order is contractual. (B.3) org_user_ids depends on OTHER users' sys_member rows, so a sys_member write must retire every entry for that ORG, not the written user's. Also: sys_session must stay OUT of leg B's watched set because enforceSessionControls writes last_activity_at once a minute per session, which under coarse invalidation would destroy the cache every minute. And explain-engine plus runAs automation must bypass the cache -- an explainer answering from cache explains a state that no longer exists, at exactly the moment an admin is verifying a revocation. Form: judged ADR-class in SUBSTANCE but not yet ripe, because two load-bearing premises are unlanded rulings (#10348-C dispatched-not-merged; #11663 awaiting ruling) and docs/adr/** is governed; proposed that the first follow-up converts it to an ADR once both settle. Hence pr: null, no draft PR, no governed surface touched.",
  "tests": "NO CODE WAS WRITTEN, so no gates are owed; this is a measurement record for a design. MEASUREMENT BASE: full (non-shallow, verified `git rev-parse --is-shallow-repository` = false) worktree cut from origin/main at 992161b728. origin/main moved one commit during the round (88b9d749a1, plugin-audit sys_activity vocabulary); `git diff --name-only` shows it touches ONLY plugin-audit objects/tests/translations, none of the files cited, so every measurement stands at both shas. `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main` exit 0. ZERO-HIT CLAIMS CARRY POSITIVE CONTROLS, exit codes captured BEFORE any pipe: (1) cookieCache repo-wide -- `git grep -n cookieCache > /tmp/cc.txt; E1=$?` gave exit=1 lines=0, and the control on the SAME instrument (`git grep -n customSession -- .../auth-manager.ts`) gave exit=0 lines=10, so the zero is a real absence and not a broken channel. (2) module-level caches on the authz path -- `git grep '^const .*= new WeakMap' -- packages/core/src/security/*.ts` exit=0 hits=1 (only #10221's localizationFailureCache), control over packages/*/src/** exit=0 hits=6. That control is what surfaced plugin-security/src/auto-org-admin-grant.ts:209 permissionSetIdCache -- an existing UN-invalidated, un-TTL'd process-lifetime cache on the authorization path; searched before treating it as new and found it ALREADY FILED as #11670 (open, bug, priority:p2), so nothing was filed. STATIC MEASUREMENTS, each read at a named line rather than recalled: resolve-authz-context.ts:319-630 (leg B's 4 waves, the isGrantActive/nowMs clock dependency, the limit-1000 fellow-org read, the seed handling and the needsUserRow condition); :648-828 (leg C, #10221's failure-ONLY cache and the getMany path); auth-manager.ts:3029-3140 (customSession's isPlatformAdmin doing an unfiltered `sys_permission_set limit 50` full page, plus activeOrgRoles) and :5734-5812 (enforceSessionControls' once-a-minute last_activity_at write and the revoke-by-writing-the-row mechanism); protocol.ts:5992-6120 (getMetaItems' queryByOrg(null) THEN queryByOrg(orgId), each with an alt-type retry on empty, plus the overlay-hydration branch that registers rows back into the SchemaRegistry -- the trap a naive leg-D cache hits); security-plugin.ts:815-845/:986-993/:1385-1400/:4320-4360 (the writeEpoch prior art and its own argument for why an epoch and not object identity); settings-service.ts:621/:767/:1180-1270/:1435/:1708/:2146 (the pre-existing subscribe/emitChange bus, the getMany two-load grouping, loadRows, and the fact that the event carries no tenant discriminator); objectql/src/engine.ts:1842 (OperationContext carries `object` + `operation`); plugin-auth/src/objectql-adapter.ts:689-691 (better-auth routes its writes through the engine -- the fact that makes the seam decisive); service-cluster-redis/src/pubsub.ts:78-92 and content/docs/kernel/cluster.mdx section 4.2 (at-most-once, no replay, 'no shipped driver provides at-least-once yet'); service-cluster/src/metadata-cluster-bridge-plugin.ts (the bridge silently returns when no cluster service is registered). CALL-SITE CENSUS: `git grep` for the three resolvers returns 17 non-test call sites across 12 packages, which is what identified explain-engine.ts:473 and service-automation/src/plugin.ts:812 as the two that must bypass the cache. RE-MEASURED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED, as the brief required: the card asserts the #10221 dogfood pin is satisfied by invalidation-on-write. Read analytics-timezone.dogfood.test.ts in full -- the write is a real PUT /api/settings/localization, the read is a SEPARATE HTTP request, and both run in ONE process, sequentially awaited. So the claim holds and is sharper than stated: a synchronous in-process invalidation satisfies it, a TTL alone does NOT (30s far exceeds the inter-request gap), and a deferred invalidation does not reliably either. That test already IS the leg-C acceptance test for 'write-invalidation primary'. PIN HARNESS REUSE VERIFIED: makeRecordingQl is `export`ed from resolve-authz-context.batch-equivalence.test.ts and counts real legs, so the identity pins can reuse it inside packages/core; noted in the design that check:cross-package-test-inputs means a pin outside core needs the repo's .testkit.ts convention (8 such files exist) rather than importing the test file. NOT MEASURED, DECLARED RATHER THAN FOLDED INTO A PASS: (a) NO DYNAMIC RUN. The worktree had no node_modules (`test -d node_modules` exit 1) and a dynamic capture would have needed a full monorepo install plus a dep-closure build; at first check the verify lock showed a holder at 465s with two heavy jobs already queued (it later freed). I narrowed the dynamic leg away and DECLARE it: no rig capture, no DEBUG=knex:query trace, no positive control of my own for the X-OS-Debug-Timing instrument this round. Every design claim above is a statement about code at a named sha, which is why the narrowing is a measurement decision and not a hole -- but leg A's better-auth query COUNT (sys_session + sys_user) is carried from the card's 2026-08-21 trace and is marked NOT MEASURED inline in the document; only its MECHANISM was re-verified. (b) cloud#1521 / cloud#1518 are out of this session's repo scope and are marked NOT MEASURED in the document; the design counts queries and legs, never milliseconds, and explicitly refuses to be read as clearing the 200ms gate. (c) No ablation was run because there is no code to ablate; the design instead REQUIRES the leg-B implementation card to ablate write-invalidation and report the observed direction. DELIVERY VERIFIED, not assumed: posted comment 5394942824 was fetched back and compared byte-for-byte against the local source. Content is fully intact (probes for session-of-record.test.ts, at-most-once, min(ttl, nextBoundary), org_user_ids, cookieCache, #4785, #10348-C, Fork 4 and the session-URL footer all present). The only delta is +58 bytes: the platform APPENDED a second, bare-form `_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.a